[LocalSend]
1. Both devices are on the same Wi-Fi network;
2. Both are running LocalSend or a compatible app;
3. Both use the same port.

[MTA]
1. Enable Bluetooth and WLAN on this device (no network connection is needed);
2. A Mutual Transfer Alliance member device nearby has its brand sharing feature enabled (e.g., Honor Share, Xiaomi Share, OPPO Share, etc.);
3. MTA devices are only scanned while the Send page is visible; switching tabs or moving to the background pauses scanning.

[LocalSend]
- While the app is in the background or the screen is locked, an ongoing transfer is protected by a background long-running task and keeps running;
- Do not close the transfer notification or force-stop the app, or the transfer will be interrupted;
- Network fluctuations or the peer exiting the app can also cause failures; retry if a transfer fails.

[MTA]
- Bluetooth and WLAN must stay enabled;
- Keep the receiving app in the foreground; moving to the background stops its receive service and prevents new MTA receives;
- Switching networks or network fluctuations during a transfer may interrupt it; retry if it fails.

MTA (Mutual Transfer Alliance) has not yet been fully tested across all brands.
If a transfer fails, collect the logs and report the issue as follows:
1. Tap the More (⋯) menu at the top right of the Send page and choose "Diagnostic Logs";
2. Turn on the "Detailed logging (DEBUG)" switch on the log page;
3. Run the MTA transfer once more to reproduce the problem;
4. Save (export) the logs to a file from the log page;
5. Go to Settings > More > Feedback and choose "Email" or "Code Repository" to report the issue, attaching the exported log file.

1. Stage files on the Send page, then tap the Web icon to open the Web Transfer panel;
2. The other device scans the QR code, or opens the shown address in a browser and enters the 6-digit access code to download, with no app required.

The address only works within the same local network; web uploads require "Allow uploads" to be enabled in Settings > Web Transfer.

The web address is only reachable within the same local network and is valid for this sharing session only.
- Stopping web transfer, restarting the web service, or restarting the app invalidates the current access code;
- The address may also change after a port fallback or network change;
- The other device needs to scan again, or use the address and access code currently shown in the panel.

If it still does not open, check:
- Whether both devices are on the same network;
- Whether the full address shown in the panel was entered correctly (default port 53310, a temporary port is used when it is occupied);
- Whether the router has guest network isolation enabled or blocks the connection.
